{"parentUuid":"b0290abf-8704-4cdc-9cec-b1fb069e2743","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/quillmark","sessionId":"buried-08","version":"2.0.17","gitBranch":"docs/themes-guide","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_01YbLWLE3eBY6EvnG7JAT4Dl","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Three built-in themes (paper, ink, sepia), each with body and heading fonts and three colours, and custom themes are TOML files like brochure.toml. The fonts page links to ../themes/ already, so the URL is settled. Outline:\n\n1. What a theme sets.\n2. The built-in themes, in a table.\n3. Choosing a theme with -theme.\n4. Paper and ink side by side.\n5. Custom themes: a TOML file, its fields, and where Quillmark looks for it."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":380,"output_tokens":287}},"uuid":"816c4650-3fe6-4c65-ab0e-f48fef1028b3","timestamp":"2026-10-10T13:58:44.000Z","requestId":"req_011CwuFgJmU4qa1tAQexVW3F"}
{"parentUuid":"816c4650-3fe6-4c65-ab0e-f48fef1028b3","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/quillmark","sessionId":"buried-08","version":"2.0.17","gitBranch":"docs/themes-guide","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_01ZY0YfNANtabrNIb6jasvBK","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DRh8IPzDRar6zc20u1yCOD","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/dev/quillmark/docs/content/guide/themes.md","content":"---\ntitle: Themes\nweight: 30\ndescription: Choose a built-in theme or write your own.\n---\n\nA theme sets the fonts and colours of a document: the body font, the heading\nfont, the colour of the text, the background and an accent colour for links\nand rules. It can also set the page size and margins.\n\n## Built-in themes\n\n| Theme | Body font | Headings | Background |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `paper` | Source Serif 4 | Source Sans 3 | white |\n| `ink` | Source Sans 3 | Source Sans 3 | near black |\n| `sepia` | Source Serif 4 | Source Serif 4 | warm cream |\n\n## Choose a theme\n\nPass `-theme` with the name of a theme:\n\n```sh\nquill render -theme ink -o notes.pdf notes.md\n```\n\nWithout `-theme`, Quillmark uses `paper`.\n\n## Compare the themes\n\nThe same page in `paper` and in `ink`:\n\n<div class=\"theme-pair\">\n  <figure>\n    <img src=\"/img/themes/paper.png\" alt=\"A page rendered with the paper theme\">\n    <figcaption>paper</figcaption>\n  </figure>\n  <figure>\n    <img src=\"/img/themes/ink.png\" alt=\"The same page rendered with the ink theme\">\n    <figcaption>ink</figcaption>\n  </figure>\n</div>\n\n## Custom themes\n\nA custom theme is a TOML file. Save it as `themes/<name>.toml` next to your\ndocument and pass its name to `-theme`:\n\n```toml\nname = \"harbour\"\nbody = \"Source Serif 4\"\nheadings = \"Source Sans 3\"\nink = \"#1d2733\"\nbackground = \"#ffffff\"\naccent = \"#0b4f6c\"\n```\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","usage":{"input_tokens":577,"output_tokens":572}},"uuid":"08288599-4753-45f4-a62f-464ce026268f","timestamp":"2026-10-10T13:58:48.000Z","requestId":"req_011CJx7wDYNKaCXJNCfjNJ8g"}
